2:T744,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"LocalBusiness","name":"GreenPoint Maintenance Services - Yonkers","description":"School cleaning refers to the professional janitorial and sanitization services specifically designed for K-12 schools, charter schools, private academies, and university facilities. Unlike standard commercial cleaning, school cleaning requires CDC-compliant disinfection protocols, exclusively non-toxic and allergy-safe products approved for environments where children are present, flexible scheduling around academic calendars, and documented compliance that satisfies health department inspections and school board oversight. GreenPoint Maintenance Services provides MBE-certified school cleaning in Yonkers and throughout New York with real-time ATP bioluminescence verification through JaniTrack.","url":"https://greenpointms.com/locations/new-york/yonkers/school-cleaning/","telephone":"+1-347-332-9348","email":"info@greenpointms.com","areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Yonkers","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"New York"}},"serviceType":"Schools & Educational Facilities","priceRange":"$","hasOfferCatalog":{"@type":"OfferCatalog","name":"School Cleaning Services","itemListElement":[{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"CDC-compliant classroom sanitization protocols"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Cafeteria and gymnasium deep cleaning"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Non-toxic, allergy-safe products for children"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Flexible after-hours and summer scheduling"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Locker room and restroom rotation programs"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Athletic facility and playground maintenance"}}]}}3:Tfde,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is professional school cleaning?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Professional school cleaning refers to specialized janitorial and sanitization services designed for K-12 schools and educational facilities. It differs from standard commercial cleaning by requiring CDC-compliant disinfection protocols, exclusively non-toxic products safe for children, scheduling flexibility around academic calendars, and documented compliance for health department inspections. Professional school cleaning covers classrooms, cafeterias, restrooms, gymnasiums, administrative areas, and specialty spaces like science labs and art rooms."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should schools be professionally cleaned?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Schools require daily cleaning during the academic year including classroom sanitization, restroom deep cleaning (twice daily minimum), cafeteria cleaning after each meal, and high-touch surface disinfection. Restrooms in high-enrollment schools need mid-day spot checks. Seasonal deep cleaning during summer, winter, and spring breaks addresses floor refinishing, carpet extraction, window washing, and HVAC maintenance that cannot be performed while school is in session."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What cleaning products are safe for schools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"School environments require Green Seal certified or EPA Safer Choice products that are non-toxic, fragrance-free, and allergy-safe. These products meet CDC guidelines for educational facility disinfection while avoiding the VOCs, fragrances, and chemical irritants that trigger asthma and allergies in children. GreenPoint uses exclusively certified products in all school facilities — we never substitute conventional products regardless of availability."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are you approved to clean NYC public schools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. GreenPoint Maintenance Services is an NYC DOE Approved Vendor, authorized to provide cleaning products and services to New York City public schools. We are also MBE/MWBE certified with NYC SBS and New York State, and SAM.gov registered for federal contracts. Every dollar spent with GreenPoint counts toward your school or district's diversity procurement targets."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you verify cleaning quality in schools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our JaniTrack system provides objective verification through timestamped, GPS-tagged photo documentation of every cleaning session, ATP bioluminescence testing that scientifically measures surface cleanliness, digital task completion checklists, and periodic supervisor audits. School administrators access all reports through an online dashboard — providing the documentation trail that health inspectors, school boards, and parents expect."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you clean around the school schedule?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We offer after-hours (evening), overnight, and weekend cleaning that never disrupts instructional time. Day porter services are available during school hours for restroom monitoring, cafeteria turnovers, and spill response. Summer deep cleaning programs are planned months in advance to maximize the break window. Our scheduling adapts to your academic calendar, exam periods, event schedules, and building access policies."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does school cleaning cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"School cleaning typically ranges from $0.08-$0.18 per square foot per cleaning visit depending on facility size, age, cleaning frequency, and scope. A typical 30,000 sq ft elementary school cleaned 5 days per week runs approximately $3,000-$6,000 per month. Summer deep cleaning is priced separately as a project. We provide detailed, scope-specific proposals after a complimentary facility walkthrough — never generic estimates."}}]}6:["stateSlug","new-york","d"]
7:["citySlug","yonkers","d"]
8:["industrySlug","school-cleaning","d"]
a:T5d4,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"LocalBusiness","name":"GreenPoint Maintenance Services Corp","description":"MBE-certified commercial janitorial and facility maintenance for schools, healthcare, churches, daycare, government buildings, and offices across NY, NJ, CT, PA, and FL.","url":"https://greenpointms.com","telephone":"+1-347-332-9348","email":"info@greenpointms.com","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Bronx","addressRegion":"NY","addressCountry":"US"},"areaServed":[{"@type":"State","name":"New York"},{"@type":"State","name":"New Jersey"},{"@type":"State","name":"Connecticut"},{"@type":"State","name":"Pennsylvania"},{"@type":"State","name":"Florida"}],"priceRange":"$","foundingDate":"2018","numberOfEmployees":{"@type":"QuantitativeValue","minValue":80},"naics":"561720","knowsAbout":["Commercial Janitorial","Disinfection","Floor Care","Day Porter","Facility Maintenance","Post-Construction Cleanup"],"hasCredential":[{"@type":"EducationalOccupationalCredential","credentialCategory":"certification","name":"Minority Business Enterprise (MBE) — NYC & NYS"},{"@type":"EducationalOccupationalCredential","credentialCategory":"certification","name":"MWBE Certified"},{"@type":"EducationalOccupationalCredential","credentialCategory":"registration","name":"SAM.gov Registered Federal Contractor"},{"@type":"EducationalOccupationalCredential","credentialCategory":"certification","name":"NYC Department of Education (DOE) Approved Vendor"}],"sameAs":[]}b:T452,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"GreenPoint Maintenance Services Corp","legalName":"GreenPoint Maintenance Services Corp","url":"https://greenpointms.com","logo":"https://greenpointms.com/favicon.ico","description":"MBE-certified commercial janitorial and facility maintenance serving schools, healthcare, churches, daycare, government buildings, and offices across NY, NJ, CT, PA, and FL.","telephone":"+1-347-332-9348","email":"info@greenpointms.com","foundingDate":"2018","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"1420 Outlook Ave","addressLocality":"Bronx","addressRegion":"NY","postalCode":"10465","addressCountry":"US"},"areaServed":[{"@type":"State","name":"New York"},{"@type":"State","name":"New Jersey"},{"@type":"State","name":"Connecticut"},{"@type":"State","name":"Pennsylvania"},{"@type":"State","name":"Florida"}],"knowsAbout":["Commercial Janitorial","Disinfection & Sanitization","Floor Care","Day Porter Services","Facility Maintenance","Post-Construction Cleanup"],"numberOfEmployees":{"@type":"QuantitativeValue","minValue":80},"naics":"561720"}0:["zD84zgCHYzEIZPbtDt1yS",[[["",{"children":["locations",{"children":[["stateSlug","new-york","d"],{"children":[["citySlug","yonkers","d"],{"children":[["industrySlug","school-cleaning","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"stateSlug\":\"new-york\",\"citySlug\":\"yonkers\",\"industrySlug\":\"school-cleaning\"}",{}]}]}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["locations",{"children":[["stateSlug","new-york","d"],{"children":[["citySlug","yonkers","d"],{"children":[["industrySlug","school-cleaning","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://greenpointms.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"New York\",\"item\":\"https://greenpointms.com/locations/new-york/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Yonkers\",\"item\":\"https://greenpointms.com/locations/new-york/yonkers/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":4,\"name\":\"School Cleaning\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$3"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Service\",\"name\":\"School Cleaning in Yonkers, NY\",\"description\":\"CDC-compliant cleaning for K-12 schools, charter schools, private academies, and universities. Green Seal certified products safe for students and staff.\",\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"LocalBusiness\",\"name\":\"GreenPoint Maintenance Services Corp\",\"telephone\":\"+1-347-332-9348\",\"url\":\"https://greenpointms.com\"},\"areaServed\":{\"@type\":\"City\",\"name\":\"Yonkers\",\"containedInPlace\":{\"@type\":\"State\",\"name\":\"New York\"}},\"serviceType\":\"Schools & Educational Facilities\"}"}}],["$","$L4",null,{"title":["School Cleaning"," Services in ","Yonkers",", ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#2ecc71"},"children":"NY"}]],"subtitle":"School cleaning refers to the professional janitorial and sanitization services specifically designed for K-12 schools, charter schools, private academies, and university facilities. Unlike standard commercial cleaning, school cleaning requires CDC-compliant disinfection protocols, exclusively non-toxic and allergy-safe products approved for environments where children are present, flexible scheduling around academic calendars, and documented compliance that satisfies health department inspections and school board oversight. GreenPoint Maintenance Services provides MBE-certified school cleaning in Yonkers and throughout New York with real-time ATP bioluminescence verification through JaniTrack.","breadcrumbs":[{"label":"New York","href":"/locations/new-york/"},{"label":"Yonkers","href":"/locations/new-york/yonkers/"},{"label":"School Cleaning"}],"heroIcon":"school","sections":[{"label":"What Is School Cleaning","heading":"Schools & Educational Facilities in Yonkers, NY","body":"School cleaning refers to the professional janitorial and sanitization services specifically designed for K-12 schools, charter schools, private academies, and university facilities. Unlike standard commercial cleaning, school cleaning requires CDC-compliant disinfection protocols, exclusively non-toxic and allergy-safe products approved for environments where children are present, flexible scheduling around academic calendars, and documented compliance that satisfies health department inspections and school board oversight.\n\nGreenPoint Maintenance Services provides professional school cleaning services throughout Yonkers and Westchester County. As an MBE-certified commercial cleaning company serving New York since 2018, we combine EPA-registered products, electrostatic application technology, and ATP bioluminescence verification to deliver measurable, documented results for every facility we serve.","features":["CDC-compliant classroom sanitization protocols","Cafeteria and gymnasium deep cleaning","Non-toxic, allergy-safe products for children","Flexible after-hours and summer scheduling","Locker room and restroom rotation programs","Athletic facility and playground maintenance"]},{"label":"Why Yonkers Businesses Need School Cleaning","heading":"Why Businesses in Yonkers Need Professional School Cleaning","body":"Facilities in Yonkers, NY face increasing pressure to maintain safe, hygienic environments for employees, customers, students, and patients. Professional school cleaning addresses these requirements systematically.","features":["Protecting student health — children are more susceptible to infectious disease transmission, and schools are high-density environments where pathogens spread rapidly through shared surfaces, restrooms, and cafeterias","Meeting health department and state education department inspection standards that evaluate cleaning frequency, product safety, and sanitization documentation","Reducing student and staff absenteeism — research shows that improved school cleaning protocols reduce illness-related absences by 10-15%, directly impacting academic performance and funding (attendance-based formulas)","Eliminating chemical exposure risks — conventional cleaning products contain VOCs, fragrances, and irritants that trigger asthma, allergies, and respiratory issues in children at rates 3-5x higher than adults","Satisfying parent expectations for visibly clean, safe learning environments — cleanliness is consistently rated among the top three concerns parents have about their children's school facilities"]},{"label":"How It Works","heading":"How Professional School Cleaning Works","body":"Our school cleaning process follows a systematic, six-step protocol designed to maximize pathogen elimination and provide verifiable documentation of results. Every step is performed by trained, background-checked technicians.","steps":[{"step":"Classroom Sanitization","detail":"Every classroom receives daily desk and chair disinfection, floor vacuuming or mopping, whiteboard cleaning, high-touch surface treatment (door handles, light switches, shared devices), and trash removal — all using Green Seal certified, non-toxic products."},{"step":"Restroom Deep Cleaning","detail":"School restrooms receive full cleaning twice daily minimum (morning and afternoon) with mid-day spot checks in high-enrollment buildings. Each cleaning covers fixture sanitization, floor disinfection, supply replenishment, and mirror cleaning with ATP verification of high-touch surfaces."},{"step":"Cafeteria Service","detail":"Cafeteria cleaning occurs after each meal service — not just at end of day. Tables and benches are sanitized, floors swept and mopped, food service areas wiped down, and trash removed. Monthly deep cleaning includes vent hood degreasing and behind-equipment cleaning."},{"step":"Gymnasium and Athletic Areas","detail":"Gym floors receive daily dust-mopping with weekly machine scrubbing. Locker rooms and shower areas are disinfected daily with products effective against MRSA and fungal infections. Athletic equipment surfaces are wiped between uses when day porter service is included."},{"step":"Seasonal Deep Cleaning","detail":"Summer, winter, and spring breaks provide windows for floor stripping and refinishing, carpet extraction, window washing, light fixture cleaning, HVAC vent cleaning, and furniture deep cleaning that cannot be performed during the school year."},{"step":"Documentation and Reporting","detail":"Every cleaning session is documented through JaniTrack with timestamped photos, ATP readings, and task completion records. Administrators access reports through a dashboard that provides the documentation trail health inspectors and school boards require."}]},{"label":"Industries in Yonkers","heading":"Industries That Require School Cleaning in Yonkers","body":"We deliver specialized school cleaning services across every commercial and institutional facility type in Yonkers and throughout Westchester County. Each industry receives protocols tailored to its specific compliance requirements, risk profile, and operational constraints.","industriesServed":[{"name":"Public Elementary Schools","detail":"Age-appropriate cleaning protocols for young children including floor-level sanitization (children sit on floors), toy and shared material cleaning, and exclusively non-toxic products for sensitive developing systems."},{"name":"Middle and High Schools","detail":"Higher-traffic protocols for locker areas, athletic facilities, science labs, art rooms, and cafeterias serving larger student populations with more diverse facility types."},{"name":"Charter Schools","detail":"Budget-conscious cleaning programs that deliver health department compliance and parent-satisfying quality within the operating constraints of independently managed schools."},{"name":"Private and Parochial Schools","detail":"Premium facility maintenance that reflects institutional standards and tuition expectations, including chapel, gymnasium, and specialized program space cleaning."},{"name":"Universities and Community Colleges","detail":"Dormitory common area cleaning, lecture hall maintenance, laboratory sanitization, student center upkeep, and athletic facility programs for higher education campuses."},{"name":"After-School and Tutoring Centers","detail":"Evening and weekend cleaning for supplemental education facilities that operate outside standard school hours and require flexible scheduling."}]},{"label":"Key Benefits","heading":"Key Benefits of Professional School Cleaning","body":"Benefits of professional school cleaning for commercial facilities in Yonkers include:","features":["Reduces student illness and absenteeism by 10-15% through systematic pathogen elimination using CDC-recommended protocols","Eliminates chemical exposure risks with exclusively Green Seal certified, non-toxic, fragrance-free products approved for children's environments","Provides documented compliance for health department inspections, school board reporting, and parent communication through JaniTrack verification","Flexible scheduling around the academic calendar — after-hours cleaning during the school year, comprehensive deep cleaning during breaks","NYC DOE Approved Vendor status and MBE/MWBE certification that satisfies diversity procurement requirements for public school contracts","Dedicated, background-checked school cleaning crews who understand the unique requirements of educational environments"]},{"label":"FAQ","heading":"School Cleaning FAQ — Yonkers, NY","body":"Common questions about school cleaning services in Yonkers.","faqs":[{"q":"What is professional school cleaning?","a":"Professional school cleaning refers to specialized janitorial and sanitization services designed for K-12 schools and educational facilities. It differs from standard commercial cleaning by requiring CDC-compliant disinfection protocols, exclusively non-toxic products safe for children, scheduling flexibility around academic calendars, and documented compliance for health department inspections. Professional school cleaning covers classrooms, cafeterias, restrooms, gymnasiums, administrative areas, and specialty spaces like science labs and art rooms."},{"q":"How often should schools be professionally cleaned?","a":"Schools require daily cleaning during the academic year including classroom sanitization, restroom deep cleaning (twice daily minimum), cafeteria cleaning after each meal, and high-touch surface disinfection. Restrooms in high-enrollment schools need mid-day spot checks. Seasonal deep cleaning during summer, winter, and spring breaks addresses floor refinishing, carpet extraction, window washing, and HVAC maintenance that cannot be performed while school is in session."},{"q":"What cleaning products are safe for schools?","a":"School environments require Green Seal certified or EPA Safer Choice products that are non-toxic, fragrance-free, and allergy-safe. These products meet CDC guidelines for educational facility disinfection while avoiding the VOCs, fragrances, and chemical irritants that trigger asthma and allergies in children. GreenPoint uses exclusively certified products in all school facilities — we never substitute conventional products regardless of availability."},{"q":"Are you approved to clean NYC public schools?","a":"Yes. GreenPoint Maintenance Services is an NYC DOE Approved Vendor, authorized to provide cleaning products and services to New York City public schools. We are also MBE/MWBE certified with NYC SBS and New York State, and SAM.gov registered for federal contracts. Every dollar spent with GreenPoint counts toward your school or district's diversity procurement targets."},{"q":"How do you verify cleaning quality in schools?","a":"Our JaniTrack system provides objective verification through timestamped, GPS-tagged photo documentation of every cleaning session, ATP bioluminescence testing that scientifically measures surface cleanliness, digital task completion checklists, and periodic supervisor audits. School administrators access all reports through an online dashboard — providing the documentation trail that health inspectors, school boards, and parents expect."},{"q":"Can you clean around the school schedule?","a":"Yes. We offer after-hours (evening), overnight, and weekend cleaning that never disrupts instructional time. Day porter services are available during school hours for restroom monitoring, cafeteria turnovers, and spill response. Summer deep cleaning programs are planned months in advance to maximize the break window. Our scheduling adapts to your academic calendar, exam periods, event schedules, and building access policies."},{"q":"How much does school cleaning cost?","a":"School cleaning typically ranges from $0.08-$0.18 per square foot per cleaning visit depending on facility size, age, cleaning frequency, and scope. A typical 30,000 sq ft elementary school cleaned 5 days per week runs approximately $3,000-$6,000 per month. Summer deep cleaning is priced separately as a project. We provide detailed, scope-specific proposals after a complimentary facility walkthrough — never generic estimates."}]},{"label":"Why GreenPoint","heading":"Why Yonkers Facilities Trust GreenPoint for School Cleaning","body":"GreenPoint Maintenance Services is an MBE/MWBE-certified, NYC DOE Approved Vendor serving over 500 commercial facilities across New York and four additional states. Our JaniTrack verification system provides the objective, documented proof of cleaning quality that facility managers, health inspectors, and building occupants demand.","stats":[{"number":"98%","label":"Client Retention"},{"number":"500+","label":"Facilities Served"},{"number":"5","label":"States Covered"},{"number":"MBE","label":"Certified"}]}],"relatedLinks":[{"href":"/locations/new-york/yonkers/church-cleaning/","label":"Church Cleaning in Yonkers","icon":"church"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/yonkers/medical-office-cleaning/","label":"Medical Office Cleaning in Yonkers","icon":"medical"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/yonkers/daycare-cleaning/","label":"Daycare Cleaning in Yonkers","icon":"baby"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/yonkers/government-building-cleaning/","label":"Government Cleaning in Yonkers","icon":"landmark"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/yonkers/office-cleaning/","label":"Office Cleaning in Yonkers","icon":"building"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/bronx/school-cleaning/","label":"School Cleaning in Bronx","icon":"school"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/manhattan/school-cleaning/","label":"School Cleaning in Manhattan","icon":"school"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/brooklyn/school-cleaning/","label":"School Cleaning in Brooklyn","icon":"school"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/queens/school-cleaning/","label":"School Cleaning in Queens","icon":"school"},{"href":"/locations/new-york/staten-island/school-cleaning/","label":"School Cleaning in Staten Island","icon":"school"}]}]],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L5",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","locations","children","$6","children","$7","children","$8","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L9",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L5",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","locations","children","$6","children","$7","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L9",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L5",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","locations","children","$6","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L9",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L5",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","locations","c